mexico city's latest effort to stop us  still rampaging kovid 19  rapid testing booths set up in points  around the capital  like this one outside the famous azteca  football stadium  they're free although the results take  about five days to arrive  chef manuel lopez wishes they'd been  available much earlier  it's been done but perhaps this should  have come sooner it would have helped to  prevent this pandemic because we needed  this many months before  that way we would have avoided a lot  more infections  the city governments also introduced  these qr codes  which registered the phone numbers of  customers at shops and restaurants  so they can be told if they've come into  contact with anyone infected  this is the way to stop the virus the  capital's authorities  have finally concluded testing and  tracing  just like the world health organization  said months ago  but outside of mexico city the federal  government still isn't convinced  the country's got one of the lowest  testing rates in the world  and the coronavirus sar says that after  a certain point  tracing doesn't really work  meanwhile the mexican death rate is one  of the highest in the world 800 more  fatalities were announced just on  wednesday  and more than 100 000 people have died  in total  and things are getting worse not better  but president andres manuel lopez  obrador is still not convinced that a  police lockdown is the answer  its effectiveness hasn't been fully  demonstrated  many times lockdowns are carried out to  exalt the authoritarian attitude of an  official  you have to trust the people many in the  informal sector  which makes up more than half of  mexico's workforce would agree with him  they have no safety net if they're  forced to stay home and the government  hasn't brought out a wide-ranging aid  package to help them  they have to go out and work what the  government has put money into  is hospital beds so far mexico hasn't  run out of those  there are however a lot of questions  over the quality of equipment  and the service the overstretched  medical staff are able to provide  and the infections go on john holman al  jazeera mexico city
 

